  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "At the 98th Academy Awards on March 15, 2026, the Best Live Action Short Film category ended in a rare tie between \"The Singers\" (directed by Sam A. Davis and Jack Piatt) and \"Two People Exchanging Saliva\" (directed by Alexandre Singh and Natalie Musteata), as reported by The Hollywood Reporter. Here are the details on the 2026 Live Action Short Film winners and nominees: Winners: \"The Singers\" (USA) — A lively, emotional short regarding community vocalists, directed by Sam A. Davis and Jack Piatt, according to Gateway Film Center. \"Two People Exchanging Saliva\" (France/USA) — A provocative, minimalist piece directed by Alexandre Singh and Natalie Musteata, notes Gateway Film Center. Nominees: \"Butcher's Stain\" (Israel/USA) — Directed by Meyer Levinson-Blount & Oron Caspi, a tense drama about workplace pressure. \"A Friend of Dorothy\" (USA) — Directed by Lee Knight & James Dean, a heartfelt film on connection and identity. \"Jane Austen's Period Drama\" (UK/USA) — Directed by Steve Pinder & Julia Aks, a satire of classic storytelling. Key Details: The tie was presented by Kumail Nanjiani, notes KTLA. This is the seventh tie in Academy history, according to KTLA. The ceremony was held at the Dolby Theatre, as reported by KTLA.",
